    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0035" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v17/pg3"/>

                <head>2. Note From Secretary of State Dulles to Secretary-General
                        Hammarskjöld<anchor n="1" xml:id="d2-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1956-12-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                    1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Hammarskjold</hi>: I enclose herewith a copy
                    of the informal memorandum which I used as a sort of a talking paper with you
                    this afternoon in relation to the putting up of funds to help finance the
                    reopening of the Suez Canal.</p>
                <p>It was a very great pleasure to have seen you and to have had the good talk with
                    you.</p>
                <p>With best wishes for a good New Year.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">John Foster Dulles</hi><anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d2-f2"/></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d2-a1.xml" xpointer="d2-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d2-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d2-f1-content">
                <p>Source: USUN Files, Unnumbered Files, Suez Canal. According to the notes of the
                    Secretary’s Staff Meeting for January 3, this note and the enclosure were not
                    delivered to Hammarskjöld until January 2. (Department of State, Secretary’s
                    Staff Meetings: Lot 63 D 75)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d2-f2" n="2" xml:id="d2-f2-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
